    "updated_at": "2026-02-19T09:13:09Z",
    "body": "> namely that it <details open during parse should not trigger a cancellable beforetoggle event. Otherwise it should be cancelable.\n\nI don't think we want it to fire *any* 'beforetoggle' event right, even a non-cancellable one? Synchronous events fired as part of parsing feels wrong.",
