    "created_at": "2026-02-19T09:18:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-02-19T09:18:31Z",
    "body": "Right now `<dialog open>` doesn't trigger `beforetoggle`, in fact `dialog.toggleAttribute('open', true)` doesn't either. The only path for Dialogs & Popovers to trigger `beforetoggle` is via script (`.show()`/`.showModal()`/`.close()`/`.showPopover()`/`.togglePopover()`/`.hidePopover()`) or via UI (`popovertarget` or `commandfor`).\n\nSo for `<details>` to match this behaviour it would need an API in script, e.g. `.open()` and `.close()`), _or_ we'd need to fire events on setting of the attribute, but doing that would also require us to have some odd guards to prevent events firing during parse, for example we could check if the document is fully active before firing, that might be very odd though.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
