    "updated_at": "2026-02-19T09:56:46Z",
    "body": "> I'm not sure what the equivalent spec mechanism for this is but WebKit has a \"finishParsingChildren\", I believe we could set a flag on the details element once this fires and conditionally fire the beforetoggle event based on that flag?\n\nRefs https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11781\n\n> One other complexity is around cancelability when say details close based on the name attribute algorithm, do we want that close to be cancelable?\n\nI think removing an attribute should not be cancelable, and if you for example cancel the close but the open attribute remains that's a weird state, so it should not be cancelable in the cases of attribute change, but _could_ be cancelable via script if we added IDL. ",
