    "body": "How does the toggle event behave on parsing? From my perspective as a web developer, I would expect beforetoggle to fire for each toggle that would also fire a toggle event, but never when a toggle event wouldn't fire. I agree firing synchronous events as part of parsing would feel weird.\n\nI haven't gone to check how the toggle event behaves during parsing, but my naive expectation is that it wouldn't fire at that time because the `<details>` element is simply appearing in its initial state rather than toggling. If I really felt a need to somehow handle `<details>` elements being added to the DOM already in an open state I would be looking at the `MutationObserver` API for that rather than toggle or beforetoggle events.",
